From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Beanjar <beanjar@invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:20:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] avutil/hwcontext_v4l2request: Define Raspberry Pi
 NV12MT_COL128 formats

The Raspberry Pi HEVC decoder (rpi-hevc-dec) offers only the downstream
NV12MT_COL128 ('Nc12'), NV12MT_10_COL128 ('Nc30'), NV12_COL128 ('NC12')
and NV12_10_COL128 ('NC30') CAPTURE formats. These are not in mainline
linux/videodev2.h, so with distribution kernel headers the SAND128 table
entries compile out and no CAPTURE format can be selected.

Define the two formats with separate luma and chroma buffers when the
headers lack them. The single-buffer ones stay undefined, because with
those the driver uses the old downstream slice bit_size meaning.
---
 libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c b/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
index b6633d9081bc7aa16141ff9b1eb5656289db1fc3..87986bdeac0c579031ae6fc2afb99cbbda0d8da5 100644
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
@@ -34,6 +34,23 @@
 #include "hwcontext_v4l2request_internal.h"
 #include "mem.h"
 
+/*
+ * The Raspberry Pi HEVC decoder (rpi-hevc-dec) CAPTURE formats are only
+ * defined in the downstream Raspberry Pi kernel headers. Define the variants
+ * with separate luma and chroma buffers ('Nc12', 'Nc30') here, so support
+ * does not depend on the headers of the build host. The single-buffer
+ * NV12_COL128 and NV12_10_COL128 ('NC12', 'NC30') are deliberately left
+ * undefined: with those the driver takes slice bit_size in its old
+ * downstream meaning (data_byte_offset included), which this hwaccel does
+ * not use.
+ */
+#ifndef V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12MT_COL128
+#define V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12MT_COL128 v4l2_fourcc('N', 'c', '1', '2')
+#endif
+#ifndef V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12MT_10_COL128
+#define V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12MT_10_COL128 v4l2_fourcc('N', 'c', '3', '0')
+#endif
+
 typedef struct V4L2RequestVideoDecoder {
     dev_t media_dev;
     dev_t video_dev;
